# Archfile — pacman + AUR manifest for Omarchy (Arch Linux) boxes.
# The Linux counterpart of Brewfile. Inline comments say what each package is
# for, same style as the Brewfile.
#
#   ./script/arch-bundle install   # install everything listed
#   ./script/arch-bundle dump      # rewrite from what is explicitly installed
#   ./script/arch-bundle check     # drift, both directions
#
# Only *explicitly installed* packages are listed — pacman pulls dependencies
# in on its own, and listing them would bury the signal (637 packages vs 90).
#
# Not listed because nothing installs them through pacman: Zed (upstream script,
# ~/.local/zed.app), Homebrew/Linuxbrew, and the mise-managed tools (bun, claude,
# codex, gh, node — see ~/.config/mise/config.toml). Listing them would show up
# as permanent phantom drift in `arch-bundle check`.
#
# `try-omarchy-mise` is this guest image's pinned mise. Omarchy migration
# 1786952219 swaps it for `mise-bin`, so expect that line to read as drift
# after an `omarchy update` — re-dump rather than reinstalling it.
#
# ghostty sits in the AUR section because that is where `dump` files a foreign
# package, but no repo carries it for aarch64 — Arch builds it for x86_64 only.
# Here it is a local package built from the upstream prebuilt binary, so
# `arch-bundle install` on a fresh aarch64 box falls through to `yay -S ghostty`
# and builds it from source, which is slow and needs zig.

# ----- repo -----

# What this repo's config needs and a stock Omarchy install does not have.
zsh                     # login shell; .zshenv/.zprofile/.zshrc come from this repo
zsh-syntax-highlighting # fish-like highlighting, styled by zsh/dracula-highlight.zsh
zsh-completions         # completion definitions oh-my-zsh does not ship
lsd                     # `ls` replacement, aliased in zshrc — same as the mac
bc                      # arbitrary-precision calc; the Claude/Kimi status lines divide with it
git-lfs                 # gitconfig sets filter.lfs.required, so LFS repos fail without it
git-delta               # syntax-highlighting diff pager, the SSH-friendly Kaleidoscope
meld                    # GUI three-way mergetool, wired up in gitconfig.local.linux
lazygit                 # TUI for git — same as the mac
lsof                    # backs the find_port alias in zshrc
ttf-hack-nerd           # terminal font, first choice in ghostty/config.macos
wget                    # fetch things curl's flags make awkward
tree                    # directory listing for when lsd --tree is too clever
tailscale               # mesh VPN; the omarchy.tailscale bar widget reads its status

